---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
const lastUpdated = 'May 7, 2026';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How California Curated collects, uses, and protects your information, including how we work with Google AdSense and other third-party services."
	pubDate={new Date('2026-05-07')}
	categories={[]}
	tags={[]}
	author="Erik Olsen"
	draft={false}
	hideMeta={true}
>
	<p><em>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</em></p>

	<p>
		California Curated ("we," "our," "us") respects your privacy. This page
		explains what information we collect when you visit
		<a href="https://californiacurated.com">californiacurated.com</a>,
		how we use it, and the choices you have. If you have questions, please
		<a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>What we collect</h2>
	<p>
		We collect a small amount of information automatically when you visit the
		site, primarily through standard server logs and analytics. This may include
		your IP address, browser type, operating system, the pages you view, the time
		of your visit, and the website you came from. We use this information to
		understand site usage and to keep the site secure.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you sign up for our newsletter or send us a message, we collect the
		information you provide (such as your name and email address) only for the
		purpose of replying or sending the content you requested.
	</p>

	<h2>Cookies</h2>
	<p>
		We and our service providers use cookies and similar technologies (such as
		web beacons, local storage, and tracking pixels) to operate the site,
		remember your preferences, measure traffic, and serve advertising. Most
		browsers let you control cookies through their settings, including blocking
		or deleting them. Note that disabling cookies may affect how parts of the
		site function.
	</p>

	<h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
	<p>
		California Curated displays advertising served by Google AdSense and other
		Google-certified third-party vendors. Google and its partners use cookies
		(including the DoubleClick DART cookie) and other identifiers to serve ads
		based on your prior visits to this site and other sites on the internet.
	</p>
	<p>
		You can learn more about how Google uses information from sites or apps
		that use Google's services at
		<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
			policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites
		</a>.
	</p>
	<p>
		You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting
		<a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
			Google Ads Settings
		</a>,
		<a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
			the Digital Advertising Alliance opt-out page
		</a>, or
		<a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
			the Network Advertising Initiative opt-out page
		</a>.
		Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or Switzerland
		can manage consent for personalized advertising through the consent prompts
		shown on the site.
	</p>

	<h2>Analytics</h2>
	<p>
		We may use analytics services (such as Google Analytics) to understand
		aggregate traffic patterns. These services collect information about your
		use of the site through cookies and similar means. The data is aggregated
		and is not used to identify you personally.
	</p>

	<h2>Third-party links and embedded content</h2>
	<p>
		Articles on California Curated may include links to other websites and
		embedded content (such as YouTube videos or images hosted on third-party
		platforms). Those third parties have their own privacy practices, and we
		are not responsible for the content or privacy policies of those sites.
	</p>

	<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
	<p>
		California Curated is intended for a general audience. We do not knowingly
		collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child
		under 13 has provided us with personal information, please
		<a href="/contact/">contact us</a> and we will delete it.
	</p>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>
	<p>
		Depending on where you live, you may have rights regarding the personal
		information we hold about you, including the right to access, correct, or
		delete it, and the right to object to or restrict certain processing.
		California residents have specific rights under the California Consumer
		Privacy Act (CCPA) and the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA). Residents
		of the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom have rights under the
		General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). To exercise any of these rights,
		<a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>
		We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will
		change the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Significant changes
		will be highlighted on the site or sent by email if you've subscribed.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how we handle your
		information, please <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
